{"step_index":5800,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T20:31:12Z","thinking":"Initial assessment of string pairs reveals that mismatches in the first letter consistently lead to rejection. However, near matches with identical first letters were accepted. The \"low_sim\" rejection suggests that a generic substitute was identified and rejected in the case of a similarity score below a certain threshold, but this was not the case when the words were identical.\n\n\nInvestigating the \"low_sim\" rejection for `كارنيفيتا` vs. `كارنتينا`, discovered that these are distinct commercial brands from different manufacturers, thus justifying the rejection based on the user's rule. This clarifies the expected behavior even when the terms seem very similar. Updating the system prompt to explicitly disallow brand substitutions.\n\n\nExamining the code, the system now explicitly checks for commercial prefix mismatches (\"new\" vs. \"نيو\") and performs a deterministic brand similarity check. The brand check isolates the first word of the brand and compares its cleaned form, ignoring the article \"ال\" and using a set of confusable initial letters to allow for some variations while disallowing others. This should prevent the kind of undesirable matches seen previously.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"D:\\\\AI_Engineer\\\\Pharmacy-agy\\\\src\\\\fast_match\\\\coordinator.py\"","EndLine":"25","StartLine":"15","toolAction":"\"Viewing lines 15-25 of coordinator.py\"","toolSummary":"\"View lines 15-25 in coordinator.py\""}}]}
